tpm-pin (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix PCR 7 policy bypass and enforce Esys_PolicyAuthValue.
  * Correct TPM2_SE_TRIAL value to 0x03 and realign TSS2 struct ABI sizes.
  * Add Microsoft Pluton, AMD PSP, and Intel PTT hardware fTPM detection.
  * Enable AES-128-CFB encrypted TPM sessions for bus security.
  * Thread safety: remove global TCTI and manage per-context via Esys_GetTcti.
  * Harden file I/O against symlink/FIFO attacks with O_NOFOLLOW and fsync.
  * Prevent privilege escalation on --user and resolve PKEXEC_UID/SUDO_UID.
  * Gracefully handle empty PIN inputs in PAM module and CLI.
  * Expand automated test harness and update multi-distro release packages.

 -- Secure PIN Maintainers <steace@coderage.pro>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:30:00 -0400

tpm-pin (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of Secure PIN for Linux.
  * Support for TPM 2.0 ESYS sealing, DA anti-hammering lockout, and PCR 7 binding.
  * PAM module with unified prompt and GNOME Keyring auto-unlock.
  * Native GTK4/Libadwaita settings application.

 -- Secure PIN Maintainers <steace@coderage.pro>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
